  "record_bodies_before": {
    "courier-relay/protocol-1": "Courier Relay provider protocol agreement, permanently revised by trial-llv. This existing mutable key retains its original name but describes the current agreement and supported historical version. The provider permanently adopted protocol \"2\", and the integration owner approved it as current (source: trial-llv). Omitted protocol selects \"2\"; explicit \"2\" selects the same contract; explicit \"1\" remains supported. This applies to the entire supplied receipt set regardless of receipt dates.\n\nProtocol \"2\": delivery_id alone identifies a delivery across all accounts; the same delivery_id under another account is another receipt of that delivery. Exactly one receipt is accepted per identity: latest occurred_at UTC instant, then smallest record_id for equal instants. This identity follows the provider delivery-ID allocation guarantee; account attribution alone does not change it.\n\nProtocol \"1\" (source: vendor/protocol-1.md as recorded during trial-tbx): identity is (account_id, delivery_id), so the same delivery_id in different accounts represents separate deliveries. Exactly one receipt is accepted per identity: earliest occurred_at UTC instant, then smallest record_id for equal instants.\n\nBoth protocols compare timestamps as UTC instants, including offset date-boundary crossings; record_id order is Unicode code-point order. Accepted receipts retain original fields, timestamp spelling, and payload, and appear in original input order. For count and summary, return exactly protocol (the actual version string), accepted_count (distinct identities), and duplicate_count (total receipts minus accepted_count). Winner selection cannot affect these counts, so the current count-only implementation need not select receipt winners. Empty sets yield zero counts; singleton sets yield one accepted and zero duplicates. Requests are independent, without persistence. Ping and unknown-command responses remain unchanged.\n\nVerified for trial-llv: all six supplied count_1/summary_1/summary_2 cases and unittest discovery passed. Regression coverage checks both commands with omitted/\"1\"/\"2\" protocol, empty/singleton/cross-account batches spanning 2020–2099, exact response shape, and unknown-command behavior; smoke covers ping. These checks verify counts, not winner selection. The actual earlier record, including historical verification when omitted protocol selected \"1\", is preserved at courier-relay/protocol-1/history/pre-protocol-2.",
    "courier-relay/protocol-1/history/pre-protocol-2": "Courier Relay provider protocol 1 contract (source: vendor/protocol-1.md, consulted for trial-tbx). Delivery identity is the pair (account_id, delivery_id); identical delivery_id values in different accounts represent separate deliveries. This follows the provider delivery-ID allocation guarantee; account attribution alone does not change identity. Exactly one receipt per identity is accepted: earliest occurred_at UTC instant, with smallest record_id breaking equal-instant ties. Accepted receipts retain their original fields, timestamp spelling, and payload and are presented in original input order. For count and summary, accepted_count is the number of distinct identity pairs and duplicate_count is total receipts minus accepted_count; winner selection cannot affect these counts. Verified trial-tbx cross-account CLI behavior with both omitted protocol and explicit protocol \"1\", alongside supplied summary/count suites and the smoke test."
  },
  "record_bodies_after": {
    "courier-relay/protocol-1": "Courier Relay provider protocol agreement, permanently revised by trial-llv. This existing mutable key retains its original name but describes the current agreement and supported historical version. The provider permanently adopted protocol \"2\", and the integration owner approved it as current (source: trial-llv). Omitted protocol selects \"2\"; explicit \"2\" selects the same contract; explicit \"1\" remains supported. This applies to the entire supplied receipt set regardless of receipt dates.\n\nProtocol \"2\": delivery_id alone identifies a delivery across all accounts; the same delivery_id under another account is another receipt of that delivery. Exactly one receipt is accepted per identity: latest occurred_at UTC instant, then smallest record_id for equal instants. This identity follows the provider delivery-ID allocation guarantee; account attribution alone does not change it.\n\nProtocol \"1\" (source: vendor/protocol-1.md as recorded during trial-tbx): identity is (account_id, delivery_id), so the same delivery_id in different accounts represents separate deliveries. Exactly one receipt is accepted per identity: earliest occurred_at UTC instant, then smallest record_id for equal instants.\n\nBoth protocols compare timestamps as UTC instants, including offset date-boundary crossings; record_id order is Unicode code-point order. Accepted receipts retain original fields, timestamp spelling, and payload, and appear in original input order. For count and summary, return exactly protocol (the actual version string), accepted_count (distinct identities), and duplicate_count (total receipts minus accepted_count). Winner selection cannot affect these counts, so the current count-only implementation need not select receipt winners. Empty sets yield zero counts; singleton sets yield one accepted and zero duplicates. Requests are independent, without persistence. Ping and unknown-command responses remain unchanged.\n\nVerified for trial-llv: all six supplied count_1/summary_1/summary_2 cases and unittest discovery passed. Regression coverage checks both commands with omitted/\"1\"/\"2\" protocol, empty/singleton/cross-account batches spanning 2020–2099, exact response shape, and unknown-command behavior; smoke covers ping. These checks verify counts, not winner selection. The actual earlier record, including historical verification when omitted protocol selected \"1\", is preserved at courier-relay/protocol-1/history/pre-protocol-2.",
    "courier-relay/protocol-1/history/pre-protocol-2": "Courier Relay provider protocol 1 contract (source: vendor/protocol-1.md, consulted for trial-tbx). Delivery identity is the pair (account_id, delivery_id); identical delivery_id values in different accounts represent separate deliveries. This follows the provider delivery-ID allocation guarantee; account attribution alone does not change identity. Exactly one receipt per identity is accepted: earliest occurred_at UTC instant, with smallest record_id breaking equal-instant ties. Accepted receipts retain their original fields, timestamp spelling, and payload and are presented in original input order. For count and summary, accepted_count is the number of distinct identity pairs and duplicate_count is total receipts minus accepted_count; winner selection cannot affect these counts. Verified trial-tbx cross-account CLI behavior with both omitted protocol and explicit protocol \"1\", alongside supplied summary/count suites and the smoke test."
  },
